Description: antinomie: write ELF32 cores of AArch32 programs on arm64
 The exit and manual process cores of an AArch32 task were refused
 (-EOPNOTSUPP), although the writer they run is the task's own binary
 format's: for an AArch32 program fs/compat_binfmt_elf.c's, which writes the
 file the arm64 kernel's own core dumps of such a program are, ELFCLASS32
 EM_ARM with the compat NT_PRSTATUS of user_aarch32_view, NT_ARM_VFP, the
 compat NT_SIGINFO, a 32-bit NT_FILE and auxv. On arm64 with
 CONFIG_COMPAT_BINFMT_ELF ant_core_abi_ok() (kernel/antinomie/process_core.h)
 lets core_writer.c and manual_core.c run it; ia32 programs on x86-64 are
 still refused.
 .
 process_core.c reads the program headers of either class to find the file's
 extent and its threads (core_header(), core_phdr()), and the core's status
 says which file it is: ANTC_CORE_COMPAT_ELF32 instead of NATIVE_ELF64.
 CORE_CAPS offers ANTC_CORE_CAPS_COMPAT_ELF32. No kernel file outside
 kernel/antinomie changes but the arm64 header's comment.
 .
 Contract revision 21.
Author: MikiMiku <jonathanirvinjo@gmail.com>
